WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.201
-Well, while you guys
were clapping,

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.502
the Rams punted six more times.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:05.237
-Really?
-That's right.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:08.541
That's right -- Last night
was Super Bowl LIII,

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.310
and 53 is also how many people

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.811
stayed awake
for the whole thing.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.312
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:14.947
But I want to say
congratulations

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.383
to the New England Patriots
on winning the Super Bowl.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.618
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.287
[ Booing ]

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.858
And to the Rams, who got to see
a free Maroon 5 concert.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.858
That's good.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.159
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:29.395
That's right --
The Rams only scored 3 points,

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.463
and they were totally shut out
in the second half.

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.299
They said it was a little tough
to concentrate

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.767
after seeing
Adam Levine's nipples.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:38.070
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.674
But the Rams did set
a new record for punts.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.209
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.945
This is the first time I've ever
seen a punter on the sideline

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.014
breathing into an oxygen mask.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:51.217
"You've got to be kidding me.
I'm going back in?"

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.387
[ Applause ]

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.456
That's right -- Rams quarterback
Jared Goff just couldn't score.

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.559
Americans said, "If we wanted
to see a football player

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.561
who can't score, we'd watch
Colton on 'The Bachelor.'"

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.797
I mean, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.598
-Whoa!

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.167
-Hey, at one point in the game,

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.502
I saw Tom Brady yelled out,
"Reagan, Reagan,"

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.904
and the Patriots ran the ball
to the right.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.339
Did you see that?

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.942
Then later, the Rams ran a play
called Trump,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.543
and they got sacked
by Nancy Pelosi.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.512
-Really?
Wow.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.148
[ Applause ]

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.717
-Get this -- I read that
over 10 million workers

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.052
called in sick to work today.

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:30.190
That doesn't include the 53 Rams
who skipped work last night.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.924
Oh! Hey. Whoa.
-Come on.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.259
Come on.
-Mr. Sports, huh?

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:35.961
You're being a little hard
on them.

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:37.630
What do I care?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.898
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.367
I don't care. Come on.
I don't care about this.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.435
They did a good job, I thought.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.103
-Yeah, come on.
They played a game.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.072
-Ryan Gosling was fantastic.
-Ryan Gosling was great.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.674
-I didn't even know
he was a quarterback.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.241
-Really? Wow!
-Yeah.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:50.710
-So exciting.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.712
-Well, late last night,
a reporter in Boston

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.547
was covering
the postgame celebrations,

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.781
and she said things
were starting

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:57.050
to quiet down in Boston.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.218
Watch this.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.186
-He said things were
maybe calming down a bit.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.121
People were starting to disperse
a little bit

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.422
while they are coming west.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:04.657
-Six rings, baby.
-There we go.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.626
-Six [bleep] rings!
-Okay. All right.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.961
All right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.964
-Gosh, I love Boston so much.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.866
That was actually
the mayor of Boston.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.401
-Are you serious?
-Yeah, I've seen him before.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.069
I've seen him on the news.
-Wow.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:19.439
-"Six rings, baby."

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.340
Oh, my goodness.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.242
At the end of the night,
Gronk spoke about

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.611
how many Super Bowl rings
he's won in his career.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.513
And he had a very interesting
way of breaking it down.

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:28.581
Watch this.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.282
-So my friends and I,
we were chilling,

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:31.918
and I only played
half the season

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.085
the year we got number two.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.387
So we were hanging out,

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.989
and we all decided I have
one and a half rings,

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.459
'cause I only played
half that season.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:42.128
That one -- The time we won it
the second time.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.697
And they said that rounds down
for some reason to one.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.432
And they said
if I get two rings,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.534
that means I get another ring.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.237
I'll have two and a half, and
that rounds up to three, baby.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.072
-There you go.
-I got three rings now, baby.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.974
-There you go.
-Whoo!

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.210
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:02.848
-The Rams were like,

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.651
"I can't believe we got
outsmarted by that guy."

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.752
What?

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.620
What the hell
are you talking about?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.056
What?

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.457
I saw that before the game,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.792
CBS aired an interview
with President Trump,

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:15.461
and he said some
pretty questionable things.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.196
And while we can't filter
what he says,

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.064
we can filter how he looks
when he says it.

00:03:19.064 --> 00:03:20.233
I'll show you what I mean.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.634
It's time for "Trump Filters."
Here we go.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:25.071
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.974
-You had quite the showdown
with Speaker Pelosi.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:31.510
What did you learn about
negotiating with her?

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:36.282
-Well, I think that she was very
rigid, which I would expect.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.883
She knows that
you need a barrier.

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:39.685
She knows that we need
border security.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:40.986
And on the 15th

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:43.523
[High-pitched voice] we have now
set the table beautifully

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.658
because everybody knows
what's going on.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.493
-But I read that during
the State of the Union,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.630
there's always a designated
survivor who watches the speech

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.732
from a secure,
undisclosed location.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.101
They haven't announced
who it will be this year.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.936
But some of Trump's
cabinet members

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.804
have spoken up
to say it's not them.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:01.741
For example, here's
Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.209
He said, "Not me.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.212
I plan to sit in the front row
and slowly unwrap hard candy."

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.849
-It's a Werther's.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:13.486
-[ Imitates crinkling ]

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.554
Here's acting attorney general
Matt Whitaker.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:16.421
He said, "Not me.

00:04:16.421 --> 00:04:17.623
I've been asked to attend

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.726
so my forehead can serve
as a teleprompter."

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.161
[ Applause ]

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.730
Up next is Secretary
of Agriculture Sonny Perdue.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.831
He said, "Not me.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:27.767
I'll be there
along with every member

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.335
of my all-banjo country band."

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.536
[ Applause ]

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.671
He's fantastic.
-It's all banjo.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.205
-If you get a chance,
check them out.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:34.540
-It's a banjo army.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.843
-Next is the Director of
National Intelligence Dan Coats.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:39.044
He said, "Not me.

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:41.213
I've haunted the House chamber
for 30 years.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:43.549
My soul is forbidden
to leave the building."

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:46.485
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:49.822
And finally, here's Secretary
of Education Betsy DeVos.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:53.126
She said, "I'll do it.
I'll be the designated driver."

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.595
That's nice.
-That's sweet.

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.629
-Some more news.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.931
Trump's daily schedule's
just leaked,

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.433
and he spends more than half
of his day

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:03.302
on unstructured executive time.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.603
Though to be honest,

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.805
"executive time" sounds like
what your dad calls it

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:09.008
when he takes a newspaper
into the bathroom.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:13.346
"Well, executive time.
I'll see you in 20 minutes."

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.414
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:16.882
Executive time.

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:19.251
Get this -- In a recent
intelligence briefing,

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:23.155
Trump thought Nepal
was part of India.

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:26.192
Then later Trump was like,
"I know exactly where Nepal is."

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:28.928
It's right in the middle
of Adam Levine's chest.

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.429
Yes, he has two.

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:31.831
He has two Nepals."

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.466
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:36.068
Here's another big story.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:39.805
New Jersey senator Cory Booker
just became the ninth Democrat

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.541
to announce he's running
for president.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.109
And get this -- If he wins,

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.511
he'd be America's
first vegan president.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.080
Explains some of the campaign
slogans he's been testing.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.082
Check these out.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.249
First says, "Cory Booker --

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.051
let's bring salad back
to the White House."

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:52.985
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.854
Next, there's, "Cory Booker --

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:57.189
even I don't know
what quinoa is."

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:58.991
And finally, there's,
"Cory Booker --

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.160
more refreshing than
a tall glass of nut milk."

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.097
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:06.465
-Wow.

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:09.568
-Oh, you guys, I'm now being
told that during that last joke,

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:12.104
five more Democrats announced
they're running for president,

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.373
and the Rams just punted again.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.876
For fun.
They just did it for fun.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.745
[ Applause ]

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.384
Puts a cape on.
-I can't do it.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.987
-Like James Brown, yeah.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:32.358
And then he runs out,
punts the ball again.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.327
That was an exciting day
for him, though, right?

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.761
-Good day for him, right, but --

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.930
-I mean, how many punts
do you normally do in a game?

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.299
Three, four?
-Maybe. If that, right?

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.134
-Six punts in the Super Bowl?

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:44.670
-That seems like a lot.
-He's got to be psyched man.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.572
-I think he'd be more psyched
if he made them.

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.673
-He's probably got kids.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.242
Kids are like,
"My dad's a star."

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.342
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.944
Like, "Your dad's Tom Brady?"

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.245
He's like, "No."
-"No, no, no."

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:54.579
-"I don't even know
my dad's name.

00:06:54.579 --> 00:06:57.316
He's the punter for the Rams."
-Yeah, but he's a punter.

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:59.986
He's the punting guy.
-Yeah.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:01.621
Hey, it was Groundhog Day, guys,

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:04.590
and I heard that Punxsutawney
Phil did not see his shadow,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.392
which means an early spring.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:09.262
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.766
Unfortunately, after 20 years
in the spotlight,

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:15.868
Phil got back home,
looked in the mirror,

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.703
and saw a face
staring back at him

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.572
that he no longer recognized.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:29.148
♪♪

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:38.691
♪♪

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:48.267
♪♪

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.068
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.068 --> 00:07:52.070
-Wow!
That's powerful.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.672
-Thank you.
-That was Punxsutawney Phil?

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:55.441
-Yeah, that was me.
-He came home.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.575
-That's correct.

00:07:56.575 --> 00:07:58.043
-He'd been in the spotlight
all these years.

00:07:58.043 --> 00:07:59.611
And then finally,
it's like, "Done."

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:01.147
It's like,
"Okay, you're retiring."

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:03.416
He goes home. Who is he
if he isn't Punxsutawney Phil?

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.317
-Who is he if he's not the dude
that comes out and says --

00:08:05.317 --> 00:08:06.719
-Yeah.
-Gets dragged out.

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.287
-Who gets dragged out,
but he decides.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:09.421
-He's an animal.

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:11.857
He's just kind of
in his little cage almost.

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:13.259
-Hole or whatever he lives in.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:15.194
-Yeah, little home, whatever.
-He's a groundhog.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:18.297
-Hopefully
he's treated humanely.

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:20.466
But he's --

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:24.036
A dude dressed in a top hat
will pull him out of his cage.

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:26.205
-Right, which has to be
unsettling.

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:29.408
-And he pushes him out
like the Lion King.

00:08:29.408 --> 00:08:31.010
-And says, "Do you see
your shadow, Phil?"

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.378
-He talks. He says English.

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.246
He speaks English to the animal
that can't speak English.

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.348
-No.
-Doesn't speak our language.

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:38.417
-No, he's an animal.
-He's an animal.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.486
He's like, "Feed me.
Leave me alone."

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.254
-"Leave me alone.
I'm scared."

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:43.622
-"What do you want me to do,
like sniff?"

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.091
-"See my shadow,
not see my shadow.

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:46.592
How do you determine
if I see my --"

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.494
-Oh, see if he goes back
in his cage.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:49.662
-Of course he is.

00:08:49.662 --> 00:08:51.796
-What kind of ridiculous thing
is going on?

00:08:51.796 --> 00:08:52.831
You should be ashamed.

00:08:52.831 --> 00:08:54.967
You should be ashamed
of yourself.

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.402
-You're right.
I should be.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.137
-Yeah.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:02.107
-Because I am Punxsutawney Phil.

00:09:02.107 --> 00:09:05.311
-The punter for the Rams?
-Yes.

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:07.246
-I didn't know
that was his name.

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:11.383
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:12.684
Yeah, on Groundhog Day,

00:09:12.684 --> 00:09:15.287
all eyes were on Pennsylvania's
Punxsutawney Phil.

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:18.023
But we've also got our own
groundhog here in New York.

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:20.559
It's true.
His name is Staten Island Chuck.

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.394
He's a little different
than Phil.

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:23.929
For instance, Punxsutawney Phil

00:09:23.929 --> 00:09:25.764
pokes his head out
at first light.

00:09:25.764 --> 00:09:28.567
Staten Island Chuck smokes
a pack of Parliament Lights.

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.802
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.802 --> 00:09:32.638
-Those are filtered.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:35.273
-Punxsutawney Phil is surrounded
by local dignitaries.

00:09:35.273 --> 00:09:37.509
Staten Island Chuck
is surrounded by 12 guys

00:09:37.509 --> 00:09:38.778
who are all named Paulie.

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:41.413
-Wow.
Paulie G., Paulie J.

00:09:41.413 --> 00:09:42.881
-Paulie.
-Hey.

00:09:42.881 --> 00:09:45.050
-And finally, Punxsutawney Phil
comes out to see his shadow,

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:46.752
whereas Staten Island Chuck
comes out and says,

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.687
"I didn't see nothing, capisce?"

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:50.556
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:54.426
And finally, the CEO of Hershey

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:57.162
says that they're fixing
the way they make Kisses

00:09:57.162 --> 00:09:59.398
so that the tips
don't get broken off.

00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:00.532
That's a good move,

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:02.134
because nobody was buying
their new product,

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.602
Hershey's Just the Tips.

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.437
[ Laughter ]
We have a great show tonight!

00:10:05.437 --> 00:10:06.906
Give it up for The Roots,
everybody.

